before:
```html
<div class="parent"><p class="child">A nested label</p></div>
```

```css
html { font-size: 16px; }
.parent { font-size: 20px; }
.child { font-size: 1.5em; padding-left: 1em; margin: 0; }
```

after:
Here, the parent’s text is 20 pixels tall.

```css
html {
  font-size: 16px;
}
.parent {
  font-size: 20px;
}
.child {
  font-size: 1.5em;
  padding-left: 1em;
}
```

The child’s text size is 1.5 times 20, which is 30 pixels. Its padding then uses that child text size, so `1em` of padding is also 30 pixels.
